\caption(Actual tiny Gaussian fit and posterior tie.)
\alttext(The native means, priors and query outputs connect the shared-covariance derivation to a hand-checkable classification example.)

> Iris measurements before fitting

The native embedded Iris frame contains150 flowers and four measurements in
centimetres, with50 rows per species. Retain the original per-species boxplots
and petal scatter as descriptive full-data exploration. These plots are not
held-out scoring evidence. Source row order and dataset provenance remain those
of dm::datasets::iris(); no external preprocessing or substitute dataset is
introduced.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lda_boxplots.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/datasets/datasets.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto d = dm::datasets::iris();
    std::vector<std::string> classes{"setosa", "versicolor", "virginica"};
    std::print("Native Iris: {} rows, {} columns.\n\n{}\n", d.nrows(),
               d.ncols(), d.head(6).to_md());
    auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(2, 2);
    for (const std::string name : {"Sepal.Length", "Sepal.Width",
                                   "Petal.Length", "Petal.Width"}) {
        std::vector<std::vector<double>> groups;
        for (auto &c : classes) {
            auto part = d.filter([&](const dm::dstruct::DataFrame::Row & r) {
                return r.get_string("Species") == c;
            });
            groups.push_back(part.numeric_column(name).values());
        }
        auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::boxplot(groups, classes, {96, 165, 250});
        p.title(name).y_label("cm");
        layout.add(p);
    }
    layout.size(1000, 850).title("Original full-data Iris exploration").fit_panels().save_svg("build/lda_boxplots.svg");
}
```
