> Original four-feature fitted discriminants

Retain Species~Sepal.Length+Sepal.Width+Petal.Length+Petal.Width, all150 rows
and empirical priors. The native summary and confusion frame describe actual
resubstitution performance, not an unbiased prediction estimate. Discriminant
directions solve B*v=lambda*W*v and are normalized against within-class
covariance; positive eigenvalue trace proportions describe separation in that
criterion, not fractions of predictive accuracy or universally comparable
feature importance. With three classes there are at most two axes, so the
displayed LD1/LD2 classifier regions carry this fitted model’s class contrasts.
This is a transformed four-feature plot, explicitly distinct from a
two-original-predictor decision plot.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lda_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/datasets/datasets.hpp>
#include <datamunge/stats/lda.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::stats::LDA model(dm::datasets::iris(),
                         "Species ~ Sepal.Length + Sepal.Width + Petal.Length + Petal.Width");
    std::print("{}\nActual training confusion, actual rows and predicted columns:\n{}\n",
               model.to_md(), model.confusion_frame().to_md());
    model.plot_discriminants().size(950, 700).y_limits(-3.5, 5.5).title(
        "Original four-feature fit: actual training discriminants").save_svg(
        "build/lda_original.svg");
}
```
